# C17 (spec 2.2). Sign in with auth.http first: the HTTP client keeps the access cookie.
# Needs transformations@convert. PNG/JPEG files are easiest to send with curl, for example:
#   curl -b cookies -F targetFormat=jpeg -F 'options={"quality":80}' -F file=@photo.png \
#     http://localhost:3007/api/images/convert -o converted.jpeg

### The four pairs: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/images/convert/formats

### SVG → PNG at width 800 (the height keeps the aspect ratio)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/images/convert
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b

--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="targetFormat"

png
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="options"

{"width": 800}
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="logo.svg"
Content-Type: image/svg+xml

<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 100 50"><circle cx="25" cy="25" r="20" fill="#e33"/></svg>
--b--

### SVG → JPEG on black at quality 60
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/images/convert
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b

--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="targetFormat"

jpeg
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="options"

{"quality": 60, "background": "#000000"}
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="logo.svg"
Content-Type: image/svg+xml

<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="100" height="50"><circle cx="25" cy="25" r="20" fill="#e33"/></svg>
--b--

### An SVG with a script: 400 invalid_file
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/images/convert
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b

--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="targetFormat"

png
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="evil.svg"
Content-Type: image/svg+xml

<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="10" height="10"><script>alert(1)</script></svg>
--b--

### An option that doesn't apply (quality for a PNG result): 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/images/convert
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b

--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="targetFormat"

png
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="options"

{"quality": 80}
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="logo.svg"
Content-Type: image/svg+xml

<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="10" height="10"/>
--b--
